now prosecutors in germany have charged  a syrian doctor  with crimes against humanity allah musa  who is accused of torturing people  in military hospitals dominick kane on  skype from berlin dominic tell us more  about this one  the case against this individual relates  to his time working as a doctor  in military hospitals in two cities in  syria key cities at the start of the  civil war in that country namely homs  and damascus it is alleged that this  individual this defendant as we  can now call him was responsible for one  murder and numerous counts of torture  against numerous individuals  during his time as i say working in  those hospitals specifically  in the last few months of 2011 and the  first few months of 2012 what makes this  case particularly interesting  is that this individual went on in 2015  to come to syria to excuse me to syria  to germany  as many syrians did we know that more  than a million syrians came to this  country as  refugees and indeed the defendant  concerned claimed refugee status  and underwent procedures to certify  himself as a doctor who could work in  this country and indeed was working here  as a doctor in germany until the middle  of last year when he was arrested and  the allegations were put to him  now it is worth making the point that  the individual concerned this defendant  has the right to be presumed innocent  until proven guilty in this country  and as yet we don't know how he intends  to plead nor indeed do we know  when a potential date for his trial will  come  we know also that the german government  is now very keen to pursue those who it  believes  are responsible for allocate for crimes  committed crimes against humanity  committed in the syrian civil war  because they believe they can assert  the principle of universal jurisdiction  relating to war crimes that's what's  allowed them to charge this  particular individual they've also  charged two other individuals who were  already  in court cases one has 